{"name":"Heirloom Lilac","hex":"#9d96b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heirloom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A valued possession that has been passed down through the generations.","An old crop variety that has been passed down through generations of farmers by seed saving and cultivation, in contrast to modern cultivars used in large-scale agriculture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heirloom"},{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heirloom","blocks":[{"text":"In popular usage, an heirloom is something that has been passed down for generations through family members. Examples are a family Bible, antiques, weapons or jewellery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Soldier%27s_return.jpg/330px-Soldier%27s_return.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heirloom","wikidata":"Q16842191"},{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or viole